## Summary
Former Armenian President Robert Kocharyan and his son have been detained as part of a corruption investigation. The article frames the detention as politically motivated, suggesting Armenia's pro-EU prime minister is targeting a former political rival.

## Key Points
- Former Armenian President Robert Kocharyan has been detained in connection with a corruption probe
- Kocharyan's son has also been detained in the same investigation
- The article characterizes the probe as targeting Kocharyan by Armenia's pro-EU prime minister, a former rival


